# snrub.api layout

FastAPI API paired with Vue client (`../snrub.client`). Docker local stack: API, Postgres, Mailhog, client.

```
snrub.api/
├── app/
│   ├── controllers/   # Business logic (MVC controllers)
│   ├── core/          # Settings / config (Pydantic Settings)
│   ├── db/            # Engine, sessions, CRUDBase
│   ├── models/        # SQLModel tables + request/response schemas
│   ├── routes/        # FastAPI routers (HTTP + WS); prefixed /api
│   ├── security/      # JWT, bearer auth, role checks, OAuth
│   ├── services/      # Side effects (email, images, telemetry, …)
│   └── main.py
├── migrations/        # Alembic
├── tests/             # unit/ + integration/
├── scripts/
├── alembic.ini
├── docker-compose.yaml
├── pyproject.toml
├── pytest.ini
└── ruff.toml
```

## Layer notes

- Routes: thin HTTP/WS; auth via `JWTBearer` / `verify_*_access` (WS: `authenticate_websocket`)
- Controllers: orchestration; prefer domain results over framework coupling when practical
- Services: non-CRUD side effects and domain calculation
- Models: SQLModel table + separate Pydantic API schemas
- Auth: JWT bearer + role checks in `security/`; local email/password and Google OAuth under `routes/auth/`
- Cross-cutting: keep CORS and security headers correct for the Vue/React clients; validate request bodies via Pydantic schemas
